 | `REIMS_VGPU_WINDOW=0` | QEMU stays headless under `-display none` (QEMU reads it) |
+| `WEIMS_DISPLAY_MODE=auto` | downstream graphics policy: after the first window resize, offer aligned drawable pixels after 200 ms; wait for scanout acknowledgment, roll back once and stop adapting on a 10 s timeout; bounded to 800–4096 × 600–2160. `manual` |
+| `WEIMS_DISPLAY_MODE=fixed` | downstream graphics policy: retain the configured startup resolution while the window scales its image. Unset/`legacy` preserves existing behavior. `manual` |
 | `REIMS_VGPU_WINDOW_BORDERLESS=1` | borderless windows that fill their screens |
 | `REIMS_VGPU_WINDOW_SCREENS=1,0` | display i opens on the host screen the list's i-th entry names |
 | `resolution=2560x1600` | the mode the window opens for, and the guest is offered until the window's pixels are known (QEMU's reims-graphics-pci property; 1920x1080 by default) |
